/trips\"},{\"label\":\"Spring tours\",\"type\":null,\"url\":\"/trips\"}],\"title\":\"Travel by season\"},{\"links\":[{\"label\":\"About us\",\"type\":null,\"url\":\"/about-us\"},{\"label\":\"Blogs\",\"type\":null,\"url\":\"/blogs\"},{\"label\":\"Reviews\",\"type\":null,\"url\":\"/reviews\"},{\"label\":\"Be inspired\",\"type\":null,\"url\":\"/be-inspired\"},{\"label\":\"Asia guide\",\"type\":null,\"url\":\"/asia-guide\"},{\"label\":\"Gallery\",\"type\":null,\"url\":\"/gallery\"},{\"label\":\"FAQ\",\"type\":null,\"url\":\"/faq\"}],\"title\":\"Our company\"},{\"links\":[{\"label\":\"Room 911, 9/F, Tai Yau Building, 181 Johnston Road, Wanchai\",\"type\":\"location\",\"url\":\"/\"},{\"label\":\"+852 92907030\",\"type\":\"phone\",\"url\":\"tel:852 92907030\"},{\"label\":\"trips@tripsatasia.com\",\"type\":\"email\",\"url\":\"mailto:trips@tripsatasia.com\"}],\"title\":\"Contact us\"}],\"title\":\"Subscribe to our newsletter\"}}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1b:I[15755,[\"/_next/static/chunks/9f257ff6d9decb7c.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/5de94a3bde687d1f.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/4dae622e7a762c47.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/e493d6fd941de2ab.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/bb05b7b137d9617b.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/b91439db7363f0ed.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/8c9a5f59bb33c8f8.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/c434c044b92619ed.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/28d48890fae3ad90.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/30db9a9ade385c93.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/88031b112ed7858c.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\"],\"default\"]\n1c:I[25543,[\"/_next/static/chunks/9f257ff6d9decb7c.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/5de94a3bde687d1f.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/4dae622e7a762c47.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/e493d6fd941de2ab.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/bb05b7b137d9617b.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/b91439db7363f0ed.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/8c9a5f59bb33c8f8.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/c434c044b92619ed.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/28d48890fae3ad90.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/30db9a9ade385c93.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/88031b112ed7858c.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\"],\"default\"]\n1a:T610,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BlogPosting\",\"headline\":\"China and Nepal finally agree on Mount Everest height\",\"description\":\"In a sign of their increasingly close ties, China and Nepal have agreed at last on the height of Mount Everest, after more than a decade of disagreement and dispute. Earlier this month, the two countries made a joint announcement regarding the new measure of the world's highest peak, which sits at Nepal's border with China in the Himalayas. A recent statement declared that Everest is currently standing at 8,848.86 meters or about 29,032 feet. In the aftermath of a dreadful 2015 earthquake, geologists speculated that several Himalayan peaks, including Mount Everest, have possibly shrunk. However, the new measurement is nearly a meter higher than the formerly accepted altitude.\",\"image\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/8159ec9ee269c9c47d40044928de80826b072579-1280x300.webp\",\"url\":\"https://www.tripsatasia.com/blogs/china-and-nepal-finally-agree-on-mount-everest-height\",\"datePublished\":\"2025-12-20T11:00:00.000Z\",\"dateModified\":\"2025-12-20T11:07:48Z\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Trips@Asia\",\"url\":\"https://www.tripsatasia.com/\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Trips@Asia\",\"url\":\"https://www.tripsatasia.com/\",\"logo\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https://www.tripsatasia.com//branding/logo-horizontal.png\"}},\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://www.tripsatasia.com/blogs/china-and-nepal-finally-agree-on-mount-everest-height\"},\"keywords\":\"Everest\"}"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1d:T439,The announcement made international headlines as it marks an end to the long-running debate over the mountain's actual height. In the 19th century, Sir George Everest, the colonial-era British surveyor, initially proclaimed the peak at 8,840.07 meters or about 29,003 feet. The Himalaya's highest point was thus named after him at the behest of the Royal Geographical Society. Interestingly, Sir Everest had never actually seen the mountain himself. He was, though, responsible for hiring Andrew Scott Waugh, who made the first formal observations of the mountain, and Radhanath Sikdar, an Indian mathematician who calculated its height. Over the years, the United States, Italy, and Denmark had put forward varying estimates of the mountain's height. Nevertheless, Nepal has been rejecting them all and abstained from using the peak's colonial-era name. Instead, they accepted the figure of 8,848 meters, which was assessed by the 1954 Indian survey. As this survey had even included snow top of the rock summit, many other countries saw it as the official height for a long time.1e:T527,The new height was determined by using a combination of geodetic data received from three mechanisms: leveling instrument, gravity meter, and GPS. The teams placed a signal receiver at every station and measured how much time it took for signals to travel between the receiver and satellites — then converted that measurement into height. Nepal and China jointly processed the surveyed data and came up with the result. Although the new measure has a little practical impact, as the world's second-highest mountain K2 is roughly 237 meters lower, it can potentially serve the political purposes of Beijing. In 1960, China and Nepal signed the Sino-Nepalese Treaty of Peace and Friendship to officially ratify the border separating the two countries. At the time, critics felt that the treaty was a means for China to exert its image as a benevolent nation following the 1959 Tibetan Uprising, which resulted in the deaths of 87,000 Tibetans. Regardless, the last five decades have seen relatively friendly diplomacy between Nepal and China. Sadly, in September, reports emerged that China was constructing buildings on the Nepali land in Limi of Humla. The reports caused widespread protests outside the Chinese embassy in Kathmandu. In November, China's defense minister General Wei Fenghe met the Prime Minister of "])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"11:[\"$\",\"main\",null,{\"className\":\"min-h-screen\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$1a\"}}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-cloud-white\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L1b\",null,{\"title\":\"China and Nepal finally agree on Mount Everest height\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/8159ec9ee269c9c47d40044928de80826b072579-1280x300.webp\"}],[\"$\",\"$L1c\",null,{\"post\":{\"_id\":\"520f8d5e-f0ec-40ce-8962-57776b54d007\",\"_updatedAt\":\"2025-12-20T11:07:48Z\",\"body\":[{\"_key\":\"536aed44ada9\",\"_type\":\"block\",\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"003fb65612e6\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"China and Nepal finally agree on Mount Everest height\"}],\"markDefs\":[],\"style\":\"h4\"},{\"_key\":\"46dff1225e3d\",\"_type\":\"block\",\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"44b1cde6a43a\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"In a sign of their increasingly close ties, \"},{\"_key\":\"6960130afc27\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"cb5f80a063c7\"],\"text\":\"China\"},{\"_key\":\"660cdcd0663f\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" and \"},{\"_key\":\"9e3f39df551f\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"8784548b3b66\"],\"text\":\"Nepal\"},{\"_key\":\"f5ca382234e3\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" have agreed at last on the height of Mount Everest, after more than a decade of disagreement and dispute. Earlier this month, the two countries made a joint announcement regarding the new measure of the world's highest peak, which sits at Nepal's border with China in the Himalayas. A recent statement declared that Everest is currently standing at 8,848.86 meters or about 29,032 feet. In the aftermath of a dreadful 2015 earthquake, geologists speculated that several Himalayan peaks, including Mount Everest, have possibly shrunk. However, the new measurement is nearly a meter higher than the formerly accepted altitude.\"}],\"markDefs\":[{\"_key\":\"cb5f80a063c7\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.tripsatasia.com/destinations/china\"},{\"_key\":\"8784548b3b66\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.tripsatasia.com/destinations/nepal\"}],\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_key\":\"164e5b05aa34\",\"_type\":\"image\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-95e0501d174a39706002dbf08902312def4c2122-687x383-webp\",\"_type\":\"reference\"}},{\"_key\":\"c497f178a5d4\",\"_type\":\"block\",\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"8b8ab5a44073\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"$1d\"}],\"markDefs\":[],\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_key\":\"d82faa04cceb\",\"_type\":\"image\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-2166f6ddaf791ce01165f6d51dda26e837ea2caa-682x383-jpg\",\"_type\":\"reference\"}},{\"_key\":\"ae2158072295\",\"_type\":\"block\",\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"9595e6fdcb05\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"In 2005, a Chinese survey of Everest estimated that it rises at around 8,844 meters (about 29,015 feet). As the research was not authorized by Nepal, the country likewise refused to recognize it as the official height. Then, in 2015, multiple scientific studies suggested the mountain's elevation may have changed after the Gorkha earthquake in Nepal, which claimed the lives of nearly 9,000 people and injured over 22,000. Two years later, the Nepali government announced the grand plan of conducting its very first mission of evaluating the height of Mount Everest. As a gesture of goodwill, India immediately offered its help on the task. To protect its national pride, Nepal, which is home to another seven of the world's 14 highest peaks, replied that its specialists were more than capable of measuring the mountain on their own.\"}],\"markDefs\":[],\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_key\":\"1d062e02b317\",\"_type\":\"image\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-9f70d53526424942c46974b8cf9d93ea4d7afbbe-682x383-webp\",\"_type\":\"reference\"}},{\"_key\":\"ea157b204877\",\"_type\":\"block\",\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"39061c6dd1d9\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Prior to climbing to the summit, four Nepalese land surveyors have trained for almost two years for the mission. Finally, in May of 2019, Nepal sent its first team to measure Mount Everest. During a state visit to Nepal in October of that year, President Xi Jinping proposed the idea of jointly announcing the new height of Everest, calling the peak \"},{\"_key\":\"0813216b5e59\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"em\"],\"text\":\"\\\"an eternal symbol of the friendship between Nepal and China.\\\"\"},{\"_key\":\"4881896631b0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Nepal initially declined the offer from China but eventually agreed to make it a joint project. Last spring, China began the measurement of the mountain from its Tibetan side by sending an eight-member team to carry out the survey. They become the only team to reach the top in 2020 as the mountain was closed by both Nepal and China for climbers due to the covid-19 pandemic. Since May, the two sides have been examining their findings.\"}],\"markDefs\":[],\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_key\":\"5d5efee88153\",\"_type\":\"image\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-e1292b1bd45c1610c6c3d76a4db2de4bc3ecaffb-682x383-jpg\",\"_type\":\"reference\"}},{\"_key\":\"28b458513416\",\"_type\":\"block\",\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"30576ab06c53\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"During a virtual press conference, in which the two countries formally announced the new height of Everest, China's foreign minister, Wang Yi, addressed the mountain by its Tibetan name \"},{\"_key\":\"5aa7c66ac54b\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"em\"],\"text\":\"Qomolangma\"},{\"_key\":\"361db5d6694e\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" – probably to show its disapproval of the colonial-era name. Similarly, Nepal's foreign minister, Mr. Gyawali, referred to it as \"},{\"_key\":\"592154b43ccd\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"em\"],\"text\":\"Sagarmatha\"},{\"_key\":\"427918408475\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\", its Nepali name. Mr. Gyawali told the press, \"},{\"_key\":\"885dd6afb090\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"em\"],\"text\":\"\\\"The China-Nepal relationship will rise across the Himalayas, and it will reach a new height.\\\"\"},{\"_key\":\"260920fe36bf\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Susheel Dangol, Deputy Director General at Nepal's Department of Survey, stated, \"},{\"_key\":\"45c3d4e22676\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"em\"],\"text\":\"\\\"The project was a matter of national pride for Nepal and a prestigious undertaking for the Nepali government. I feel very proud that we were able to complete it successfully.\\\"\"}],\"markDefs\":[],\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_key\":\"eb3d63a99e1e\",\"_type\":\"image\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-13874c088e1e22545ab3d2551cd855378ec54312-687x383-webp\",\"_type\":\"reference\"}},{\"_key\":\"8359e2d0a3cd\",\"_type\":\"block\",\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"2c48e32941c4\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"$1e\"},{\"_key\":\"74bc3133f3a1\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"84b0aec68e72\"],\"text\":\"Nepal\"},{\"_key\":\"d51bb2340f27\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" to discuss issues. The agreement on the new height of Everest in the wake of the tensions can establish a diplomatic buffer between the two nations.\"}],\"markDefs\":[{\"_key\":\"84b0aec68e72\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.tripsatasia.com/destinations/nepal\"}],\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_key\":\"ade870a16473\",\"_type\":\"image\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-ee8deb4b8c70cabda45fd3d6e22f3d69e69c9797-682x383-webp\",\"_type\":\"reference\"}},{\"_key\":\"07b1157d0218\",\"_type\":\"block\",\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"6c28966d306d\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"In 2020, \"},{\"_key\":\"8584c699edcf\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"b33674ea45f2\"],\"text\":\"China\"},{\"_key\":\"963cf265a1f8\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"'s relations with its Himalayan neighbors have not been so warm. In June, conflicts with India resurfaced when unarmed troops from both countries clashed in the border area, which each side claim as their own, killing 20 Indian soldiers and an undisclosed number of Chinese combatants. China was also recently accused of building a village in a territory claimed by the Kingdom of \"},{\"_key\":\"4062661baa38\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"90e2b9780179\"],\"text\":\"Bhutan\"},{\"_key\":\"c4594d5eb9a5\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\". As regional tensions intensify, Beijing seems to have picked Nepal as its ally. China has long seen Nepal as key to its Belt and Road Initiative, which envisions highways, railroads, and other infrastructures built with Chinese financing \"},{\"_key\":\"71a20a6a89c3\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"2881c2a6849e\"],\"text\":\"across the ancient Silk Road routes\"},{\"_key\":\"1d22be114fa0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" that connected China to the West.\"}],\"markDefs\":[{\"_key\":\"b33674ea45f2\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.tripsatasia.com/destinations/china\"},{\"_key\":\"90e2b9780179\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.tripsatasia.com/destinations/bhutan\"},{\"_key\":\"2881c2a6849e\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.tripsatasia.com/trips/tibet\"}],\"style\":\"normal\"}],\"coverImage\":{\"alt\":\"China and Nepal Everest\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-8159ec9ee269c9c47d40044928de80826b072579-1280x300-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/8159ec9ee269c9c47d40044928de80826b072579-1280x300.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"excerpt\":\"In a sign of their increasingly close ties, China and Nepal have agreed at last on the height of Mount Everest, after more than a decade of disagreement and dispute. Earlier this month, the two countries made a joint announcement regarding the new measure of the world's highest peak, which sits at Nepal's border with China in the Himalayas. A recent statement declared that Everest is currently standing at 8,848.86 meters or about 29,032 feet. In the aftermath of a dreadful 2015 earthquake, geologists speculated that several Himalayan peaks, including Mount Everest, have possibly shrunk. However, the new measurement is nearly a meter higher than the formerly accepted altitude.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"everest\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-8159ec9ee269c9c47d40044928de80826b072579-1280x300-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/8159ec9ee269c9c47d40044928de80826b072579-1280x300.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-20T11:00:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"Enjoy luxurious trekking through the foot of the mighty Annapurna on this Nepal private tour. Track wildlife in Chitwan Nature Reserve and join the crowds as they take to Kathmandu's bustling streets to celebrate the annual Indra Jatra Festival. This trip is a fantastic opportunity for those looking to experience mild trekking in Nepal, or for families wanting to spend time trekking together while enjoying some of the coziest lodging facilities Nepal has to offer.\\n\\n\",\"metaTitle\":\"NEPAL LUXURIOUS TREKKING | NEPAL PRIVATE TOUR\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"china-and-nepal-finally-agree-on-mount-everest-height\"},\"tags\":[\"Everest\"],\"title\":\"China and Nepal finally agree on Mount Everest height\"}}]]}],\"$L1f\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"14:null\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"18:[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"NEPAL LUXURIOUS TREKKING | NEPAL PRIVATE TOUR | Trips@Asia\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"Enjoy luxurious trekking through the foot of the mighty Annapurna on this Nepal private tour. Track wildlife in Chitwan Nature Reserve and join the crowds as they take to Kathmandu's bustling streets to celebrate the annual Indra Jatra Festival. This trip is a fantastic opportunity for those looking to experience mild trekking in Nepal, or for families wanting to spend time trekking together while enjoying some of the coziest lodging facilities Nepal has to offer.\\n\\n\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"2\",{\"name\":\"application-name\",\"content\":\"Trips@Asia\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"3\",{\"name\":\"author\",\"content\":\"nomatech.agency\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"4\",{\"rel\":\"manifest\",\"href\":\"/site.webmanifest\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"5\",{\"name\":\"keywords\",\"content\":\"Everest\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"6\",{\"name\":\"robots\",\"content\":\"index, follow\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"7\",{\"name\":\"googlebot\",\"content\":\"index, follow, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"8\",{\"name\":\"article:published_time\",\"content\":\"2025-12-20T11:00:00.000Z\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"9\",{\"name\":\"article:author\",\"content\":\"Trips Asia\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"10\",{\"name\":\"article:section\",\"content\":\"Travel\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"11\",{\"name\":\"article:tag\",\"content\":\"Everest\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"12\",{\"rel\":\"canonical\",\"href\":\"https://www.tripsatasia.com/blogs/china-and-nepal-finally-agree-on-mount-everest-height\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"13\",{\"property\":\"og:title\",\"content\":\"NEPAL LUXURIOUS TREKKING | NEPAL PRIVATE TOUR\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"14\",{\"property\":\"og:description\",\"content\":\"Enjoy luxurious trekking through the foot of the mighty Annapurna on this Nepal private tour. Track wildlife in Chitwan Nature Reserve and join the crowds as they take to Kathmandu's bustling streets to celebrate the annual Indra Jatra Festival. This trip is a fantastic opportunity for those looking to experience mild trekking in Nepal, or for families wanting to spend time trekking together while enjoying some of the coziest lodging facilities Nepal has to offer.\\n\\n\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"15\",{\"property\":\"og:url\",\"content\":\"https://www.tripsatasia.com/blogs/china-and-nepal-finally-agree-on-mount-everest-height\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"16\",{\"property\":\"og:site_name\",\"content\":\"Trips@Asia\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"17\",{\"property\":\"og:locale\",\"content\":\"en_US\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"18\",{\"property\":\"og:image\",\"content\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/8159ec9ee269c9c47d40044928de80826b072579-1280x300.webp\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"19\",{\"property\":\"og:image:width\",\"content\":\"1200\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"20\",{\"property\":\"og:image:height\",\"content\":\"630\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"21\",{\"property\":\"og:image:alt\",\"content\":\"everest\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"22\",{\"property\":\"og:type\",\"content\":\"article\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"23\",{\"name\":\"twitter:card\",\"content\":\"summary_large_image\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"24\",{\"name\":\"twitter:site\",\"content\":\"@TripsAtAsia\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"25\",{\"name\":\"twitter:creator\",\"content\":\"@TripsAtAsia\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"26\",{\"name\":\"twitter:title\",\"content\":\"NEPAL LUXURIOUS TREKKING | NEPAL PRIVATE TOUR\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"27\",{\"name\":\"twitter:description\",\"content\":\"Enjoy luxurious trekking through the foot of the mighty Annapurna on this Nepal private tour. Track wildlife in Chitwan Nature Reserve and join the crowds as they take to Kathmandu's bustling streets to celebrate the annual Indra Jatra Festival. This trip is a fantastic opportunity for those looking to experience mild trekking in Nepal, or for families wanting to spend time trekking together while enjoying some of the coziest lodging facilities Nepal has to offer.\\n\\n\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"28\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image\",\"content\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/8159ec9ee269c9c47d40044928de80826b072579-1280x300.webp\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"29\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/favicon-32x32.png\",\"sizes\":\"32x32\",\"type\":\"image/png\"}],\"$L20\",\"$L21\",\"$L22\",\"$L23\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"24:I[68925,[\"/_next/static/chunks/9f257ff6d9decb7c.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/5de94a3bde687d1f.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/4dae622e7a762c47.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/e493d6fd941de2ab.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/bb05b7b137d9617b.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/b91439db7363f0ed.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/8c9a5f59bb33c8f8.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/c434c044b92619ed.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/28d48890fae3ad90.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/30db9a9ade385c93.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/88031b112ed7858c.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\"],\"default\"]\n25:I[5910,[\"/_next/static/chunks/dedeaa4f45d8760c.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/da5232201cce4031.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\"],\"IconMark\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1f:[\"$\",\"$L24\",null,{\"blogPosts\":[{\"_id\":\"4f375abb-3816-4289-8689-2d7f138ae9fe\",\"excerpt\":\"From late-January to mid-February, China, South Korea, Vietnam, Mongolia, and many other Asian countries celebrate the Lunar New Year or Spring Festival. The holiday sees the world's largest annual human migration as hundreds of millions of people take a journey back home, bringing the global economy to a halt and causing a crazy traffic load. It is an annual headache for retailers and importers overseas who rely on Asia as all factories shut down. While all countries that celebrate New Year emphasize family reunions, specific celebrations and rituals encompassing the holiday are unique in each nation. \",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Lunar new year\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-d217911ad9d1c2f81f424b05e87e9ef664b9fae6-1280x480-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/d217911ad9d1c2f81f424b05e87e9ef664b9fae6-1280x480.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T11:00:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"From late-January to mid-February, China, South Korea, Vietnam, Mongolia, and many other Asian countries celebrate the Lunar New Year or Spring Festival. \",\"metaTitle\":\"Lunar new year\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"how-asian-countries-celebrate-lunar-new-year\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"How Asian countries celebrate Lunar New Year\"},{\"_id\":\"319e3b60-e8db-4e39-bbe1-dfafd06d5e7f\",\"excerpt\":\"Father abandoned child, wife husband, one brother another; for this illness seemed to strike through the breath and sight. And so they died. And none could be found to bury the dead for money or friendship. Members of a household brought their dead to a ditch as best they could, without priest, without divine offices ... great pits were dug and piled deep with the multitude of dead. And they died by the hundreds both day and night ... And as soon as those ditches were filled more were dug ... And I, Agnolo di Tura ... buried my five children with my own hands. And there were also those who were so sparsely covered with earth that the dogs dragged them forth and devoured many bodies throughout the city. There was no one who wept for any death, for all awaited death. And so many died that all believed it was the end of the world.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Early morning, November 1347, Alfano Damiani woke up to the sound of Alasia, his 5 years old daughter’s heavy coughs. He gushed through the door, seeing her struggling for every breath, barely alive. He took to the streets of Sicily screaming aiuto, aiuto, only to find dozens of others hysterically running the streets, in hope for any assistance they could get. Horrified, Alfano ran back in only to see Alasia taking her last breath before she closed her eyes. Forever.\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-4e440690d18acaaabaaa6acd25695e8da6a3f1ef-1280x400-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/4e440690d18acaaabaaa6acd25695e8da6a3f1ef-1280x400.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T08:30:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"SILK ROAD ADVENTURE | SILK ROAD PRIVATE TOUR\\nFor centuries Westerners have been intrigued by the Silk Road, which was the first connection between the East and the West, conveying goods, knowledge, and messages of peace and war across Eurasia. Join this Silk Road Adventure private tour to explore the ancient trade routes the old way – overland.\\n\\n\",\"metaTitle\":\"Silk Road Private tour\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"the-plague-that-changed-the-world\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"The plague that changed the world\"},{\"_id\":\"12b5daf7-0526-4742-a21a-8143c8c88e31\",\"excerpt\":\"When Portuguese sailors observed the island of Taiwan in the 16th century, they called it ‘Formosa,’ which means ‘beautiful island’. No words or images can best describe and prove how beautiful Taiwan really is, as it is best experienced and explored when you’re actually there. To enjoy a more immersive experience, consider booking one of those custom Taiwan private tours. That way, the itinerary can be tailored according to the activities and experiences you want.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Taiwan Private tour\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-240983f2641ba82e967c7cac608be5c1c7c02999-1280x800-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/240983f2641ba82e967c7cac608be5c1c7c02999-1280x800.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T05:00:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"Taiwan is a country of diverse cultures, a rich and complex history, and pristine nature. This Taiwan private tour was designed to provide an in-depth insight into all these and is perfectly timed to coincide with the Pingxi Sky Lantern Festival when tens of thousands of Taiwanese come together to celebrate and fly paper lanterns in a wish for a better year to come.\",\"metaTitle\":\"Taiwan Private trip\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"taiwan-private-tours-a-custom-made-trip-for-you\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"Taiwan Private Tours – A Custom-Made Trip for You\"},{\"_id\":\"b02e6177-2dbc-45d2-9fd9-6ac12714711a\",\"excerpt\":\"Vietnam is a country that is full of tourist destinations, stunning scenery, exciting natural wonders, delicious food, and relaxing experiences—and the best way to enjoy your holiday here is to book a Vietnam private tour. If you want to experience everything Vietnam has to offer, then a private tour can give you that satisfaction. And yes—it’s well worth the money. Some people worry about costs when in fact, a custom tour can offer so much more value. \",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Vietnam trip\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-d7fc62a76d27c96a0af3d47ff708eb19a3e02c8c-1280x480-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/d7fc62a76d27c96a0af3d47ff708eb19a3e02c8c-1280x480.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T05:00:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"Vietnam private tours are also safer. The best tour companies that offer have years of experience and intimate knowledge of the country, so you can rest easy knowing your life is in safe, capable hands.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"metaTitle\":\"Vietnam private tour\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"here-s-what-no-one-tells-you-about-vietnam-private-tours\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"Here’s What No One Tells You About Vietnam Private Tours\"},{\"_id\":\"41716626-b7de-44ed-a187-a0324928eccc\",\"excerpt\":\"Are you planning to participate and watch the nation'sbiggest national holiday, Naadam? You may want to consider buying a Mongolia vacation package instead of taking the DIY route. Trips@Asia will help you pick destinations where you can taste and experience this traditional festival best. They will even arrange everything, including your itinerary, accommodation, domestic flights, private transportation, transfers, entrance fees, and meals so you can stay comfortable while enjoying the trip.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Naadam \",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-98259cdd1823641152c11065df86a1e3f32f3ab8-1280x463-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/98259cdd1823641152c11065df86a1e3f32f3ab8-1280x463.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T04:45:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"Where should you go to have a memorable Naadam experience? According to leading providers of Mongolia vacation packages, Ulaanbaatar is the best place for celebrating Naadam. Here are the reasons why.\",\"metaTitle\":\"Mongolia Naadam \"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"know-the-best-place-to-experience-naadam-in-mongolia\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"Know the Best Place to Experience Naadam in Mongolia\"},{\"_id\":\"96b92f62-d7d9-4a7c-8a64-6bde2d979023\",\"excerpt\":\"If there is any country in the world that will still surprise even the most well-travelled travelers, that’s Mongolia. So, if you are still pondering whether or not you should book a Mongolia vacation package, you better make up your mind now. This landlocked nation is slowly opening its gates to more tourists and is beginning to attract people from all over the world. Book that vacation while you can still see the untouched and preserved beauty of this part of the world.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"The first time in Mongolia\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-98259cdd1823641152c11065df86a1e3f32f3ab8-1280x463-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/98259cdd1823641152c11065df86a1e3f32f3ab8-1280x463.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T04:45:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"If you are curious to know how nomads live, then travel to Mongolia. The locals will let you taste outdoor camping/living their way. You will be trekking and traveling from place to place as your horses and trucks move your things and gear from one camp to another. This will surely be one of your memorable experiences.\",\"metaTitle\":\"First time in Mongolia\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"unexpected-things-for-first-time-visitors-in-mongolia-to-notice\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"Unexpected Things for First-Time Visitors in Mongolia To Notice\"},{\"_id\":\"9784202b-fda0-41b8-aacc-20df72afb149\",\"excerpt\":\"As the landlocked country opens up to the world, Mongolia is attracting more and more people to its beauty and uniqueness. There are various Mongolia vacation packages that promote the colorful culture and distinct way of life of the nomads. A trip to this country is surely worth investing in. If you are pondering what experiences you will enjoy when you visit, then take a look at the following popular Mongolia vacation packages.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Mongolia\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-98259cdd1823641152c11065df86a1e3f32f3ab8-1280x463-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/98259cdd1823641152c11065df86a1e3f32f3ab8-1280x463.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T04:45:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"A trip to Mongolia is surely worth investing in. If you are pondering what experiences you will enjoy when you visit, then take a look at the following popular Mongolia vacation packages.\",\"metaTitle\":\"Mongolia Vacation\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"mongolia-vacation-packages-be-captivated-by-the-beauty-of-mongolia\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"Mongolia Vacation Packages – Be Captivated by the Beauty of Mongolia\"},{\"_id\":\"9adde365-a1e3-4328-9eea-363133e6c99a\",\"excerpt\":\"Bhutan is a landlocked country that stretches between the Himalayan southern slopes to the north and the southern savannas and grasslands. Known as the ‘world’s happiest country’, its culture is predominantly influenced by Tibet, with the official language being Tibetan dialect and the religion as Tibetan Buddhism. Tibetan feudalism has also greatly influenced the history of Bhutan, and the fortified monasteries known as Dzongs still stand and are being used today. The best way to experience everything the country has to offer is with custom Bhutan private tours.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Bhutan trip\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-4dde6f584d8ad064c3a9e5f773134d5ef94ef70c-1280x480-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/4dde6f584d8ad064c3a9e5f773134d5ef94ef70c-1280x480.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T04:45:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"Tibetan feudalism has also greatly influenced the history of Bhutan, and the fortified monasteries known as Dzongs still stand and are being used today. The best way to experience everything the country has to offer is with custom Bhutan private tours.\",\"metaTitle\":\"Bhutan private tour\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"bhutan-private-tours-things-to-do-in-bhutan\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"Bhutan Private Tours – Things to Do in Bhutan\"},{\"_id\":\"f1b8c8d2-0b3c-4b97-98e1-619f71a97179\",\"excerpt\":\"Hiking Tours Asia – Enjoy Exciting \u0026 Exclusive Destinations in Asia\\nFor the adventurous and nature-lover, hiking is a great way to discover and explore many different places. It makes reaching your destination feel more rewarding after an exciting journey traversing varied terrain. So, if you are looking to discover Asia in a different way, consider booking a hiking tour with a reputable and trustworthy travel company. Hiking tours in Asia will take you through some of the most exclusive and exciting destinations in the continent. Amazing trails and paths with breathtaking sights and memorable sounds await you and your companions with custom tour packages available to ensure that all the places you want to see can be covered.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Hiking tour\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-667a77fb8861690b63351f82092e81dc31c82291-1280x400-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/667a77fb8861690b63351f82092e81dc31c82291-1280x400.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T04:45:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"Hiking tours in Asia are a must-experience, especially if you are a true nature lover or you are simply the adventurous type. Just be sure to plan your trip with a credible tour company, so all you have to do is pack your gear and brace yourself for uniquely designed hikes in Mongolia and other destinations.\",\"metaTitle\":\"Asia hiking tour\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"hiking-tours-asia-enjoy-exciting-and-exclusive-destinations-in-asia\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"Hiking Tours Asia – Enjoy Exciting \u0026 Exclusive Destinations in Asia\"},{\"_id\":\"4a31b3d9-3175-4eab-b7a9-bb43f46c5fc6\",\"excerpt\":\"Cultural Tours in Asia – Insight into the Way of Life of the Local People\\nThere is nothing like Asian culture, especially when you have the opportunity to behold the one-of-a-kind art, learn every country’s cultural perceptions, and get to know the way of life of the people. For a better way to get acquainted with the Asian state of mind, consider signing up for custom cultural tours in Asia. A tour package could take you through Asia’s art scene and bring you to see and learn about iconic cultural monuments. The objective of these trips is to provide an insight into the culture, understand its origins, and how it translates into the daily life of both rural and city folk.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Asian Cultural tour\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-98259cdd1823641152c11065df86a1e3f32f3ab8-1280x463-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/98259cdd1823641152c11065df86a1e3f32f3ab8-1280x463.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T04:30:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\" A tour package could take you through Asia’s art scene and bring you to see and learn about iconic cultural monuments.\",\"metaTitle\":\"Asian Cultural tour\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"cultural-tours-in-asia-insight-into-the-way-of-life-of-the-local-people\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"Cultural Tours in Asia – Insight into the Way of Life of the Local People\"},{\"_id\":\"54842d48-3028-4a0f-be3d-09efa894d8ab\",\"excerpt\":\"Whether it’s your first or nth time visiting South Korea, you may want to experience the country in a more intimate way with a private tour. Korea private tours are popular with discerning travelers looking to travel more comfortably without the stress. Traveling this way will give you more opportunities to immerse yourself into the amazing culture through personalized activities and the places you want to see and experience, without the uninteresting stops. Moreover, it will give you more control over what to see and do, whether you’re traveling alone, with a small group, or with a special someone.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"South Korea tour\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-41b497f27f16fe40643668ed3a8143f8868e2d11-1280x480-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/41b497f27f16fe40643668ed3a8143f8868e2d11-1280x480.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T04:30:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"\\nOur South Korea private tours make a perfect mix of urban and natural landscapes, old and new customs, and an up-close encounters with the Korean unique culinary world.\",\"metaTitle\":\"South Korea Private Tours\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"korea-private-tours-interesting-facts-about-korea\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"Korea Private Tours – Interesting Facts about Korea\"},{\"_id\":\"d2f7dc81-6d0b-404f-9d44-9bc647e4cb44\",\"excerpt\":\"The Best Asia Hiking Tours That You Must Try\\nAsia is home to a plethora of national landmarks and highest mountains on the planet, making it a very popular destination for adventure junkies. If you love trekking, then you should join an Asia hiking tour. Exploring this continent by foot is simply the best. It allows you to discover its culture and will make you appreciate your journey even more. This list includes some of the must-try hiking destinations on the continent and explains why people from around the globe travel thousands of miles to hit the trails there.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Asian the best hiking trips\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-9ffce11d392e336d3e4fe5d151a10333cde28fbc-1280x480-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/9ffce11d392e336d3e4fe5d151a10333cde28fbc-1280x480.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T04:15:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"Hiking \u0026 Trekking tours in Asia\\nAway from civilization, mostly in remote mountain ranges, through terrain not accessible to vehicles, we encounter pristine natural phenomenon and the tranquil beauty of a variety of landscapes, from sub-arctic to sub-tropic.\",\"metaTitle\":\"Asian the best hiking tour\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"the-best-asia-hiking-tours-that-you-must-try\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"The Best Asia Hiking Tours That You Must Try\"},{\"_id\":\"fb5891ad-0853-4dc2-a1bd-69782b4dd673\",\"excerpt\":\"Champa: The Forgotten Kingdom of Vietnam\\nThe Kingdom of Champa appeared out of nowhere and disappeared as if it had never been here. It left behind a rich cultural heritage, including thousands of relics, temples, and monuments across Vietnam and Cambodia, two of Asia's most popular destinations. Yet, many who traveled in the region heard very little, if anything, about this kingdom.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Northern Vietnam trip\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-d7fc62a76d27c96a0af3d47ff708eb19a3e02c8c-1280x480-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/d7fc62a76d27c96a0af3d47ff708eb19a3e02c8c-1280x480.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T04:15:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"INDOCHINA DELIGHTS\\nVietnam and Cambodia are two of the most fascinating countries on the Asian continent, both dramatically affected by recent history. In the mid of the 2nd millennia, both countries were the ground for some of the largest empires South East Asia has ever known. The decline of these empires has marked the beginning of French colonialization, bringing Christianity, modernization, and rapid development, which have forever changed local cultures and traditions.\",\"metaTitle\":\"Vietnam and Cambodia private trip\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"champa-the-forgotten-kingdom-of-vietnam\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"Champa: The Forgotten Kingdom of Vietnam\"},{\"_id\":\"0b23aafb-2939-442d-a02e-b36c59e623c6\",\"excerpt\":\"Tibet: A Century-long Struggle for Independence\\nBy the end of the 19th century, China's influence began to diminish in Tibet after the British took over neighboring India. With the Qing dynasty on the verge of collapse, British India sent a frontier commission to Tibet in 1903 to establish diplomatic ties, or more bluntly, to conquer the region.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Tibet independence \",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-6aeccafe80d76e7ca8b1bf79ac2d24c5c2072156-1280x480-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/6aeccafe80d76e7ca8b1bf79ac2d24c5c2072156-1280x480.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T03:45:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"A unique private tour through the Tibetan Plateau, commonly known as the Roof of the World, during the time the Tibetan people celebrate the Shoton Festival. Indulge through this private Tibet tour in the complex world of Tibetan Buddhism while taking in the mesmerizing views of the Himalayas rising high above this elevated plateau.\",\"metaTitle\":\"TIBET PRIVATE TOUR\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"tibet-a-century-long-struggle-for-independence\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"Tibet: A Century-long Struggle for Independence\"},{\"_id\":\"73d5929c-228d-427e-a8c6-d5eddba80664\",\"excerpt\":\"Mysteries behind the Nepalese royal massacre\\nOn June 2, 2001, news of a tragic event spread across Nepal that soon threw the whole country into chaos. Ambulances transported 15 members of the royal family from the Narayanhiti Palace to the military hospital the night before. Nine, including King Birendra, his wife, and two children, were shot dead. Crown Prince Dipendra was formally proclaimed king while in a coma, but died just three days later. His death marked the extinction of the main branch of the royal family.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Nepal trekking\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-2d662f1a39a7163baf1b861a8f2f3a7b50628c7a-1280x480-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/2d662f1a39a7163baf1b861a8f2f3a7b50628c7a-1280x480.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T03:15:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"This trip is a fantastic opportunity for those looking to experience mild trekking in Nepal, or for families wanting to spend time trekking together while enjoying some of the coziest lodging facilities Nepal has to offer.\\n\",\"metaTitle\":\"NEPAL PRIVATE TOUR\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"mysteries-behind-the-nepalese-royal-massacre\"},\"tags\":[\"Nepal\",\"Royal family\"],\"title\":\"Mysteries behind the Nepalese royal massacre\"},{\"_id\":\"f7f721c2-12b6-4677-b798-a3a7da5b3f5b\",\"excerpt\":\"Sherpas: Heroes of the Himalayas\\nOn May 29th, 1953, Sir Edmund Hillary became known as the first person to stand atop Mount Everest. However, he was not alone at the top of the world! Since then, over 4,000 climbers have successfully summited the mountain. We learn about the challenges they overcame in their quest to reach the world's highest peak through interviews, books, and movies. However, many of us never heard about the men who made these dangerous journeys possible- the Sherpas of the Himalayas!\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Tibet\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-4c8643860d994fbe065a512d9f6b4227d4ddaccd-1280x450-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/4c8643860d994fbe065a512d9f6b4227d4ddaccd-1280x450.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-22T03:15:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"This trip is a fantastic opportunity for those looking to experience mild trekking in Nepal, or for families wanting to spend time trekking together while enjoying some of the coziest lodging facilities Nepal has to offer.\",\"metaTitle\":\"NEPAL LUXURIOUS TREKKING TRIP\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"sherpas-heroes-of-the-himalayas\"},\"tags\":[\"Tibet\",\"Sherpa\"],\"title\":\"Sherpas: Heroes of the Himalayas\"},{\"_id\":\"5090ab63-14db-4c87-809b-4134a2e226cf\",\"excerpt\":\"Chinese Muslims: Hui and Uyghur people\\nIslam is an officially recognized religion of China. The traders along the Silk Road brought the faith to the country, which spread quickly among its people. Today, about 25 million Muslims live in the country, which represents 1.6 percent of its population.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Silk Road\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-6a52a50a6a2cfb6899a0a73d08562dddd0329889-1280x480-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/6a52a50a6a2cfb6899a0a73d08562dddd0329889-1280x480.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-21T16:30:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"Explore Islam in China on a Silk Road private tour. Learn how Muslim traders introduced Islam, its spread along Silk Road routes, and why over 25 million Muslims live in China today.\",\"metaTitle\":\"Silk Road Private Tour\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"chinese-muslims-hui-and-uyghur-people\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"Chinese Muslims: Hui and Uyghur people\"},{\"_id\":\"020e79fe-69cb-446e-a2c6-013beec0e744\",\"excerpt\":\"Is Dalai Lama Leader of Tibet?\\nOn March 17 of 1959, three squads, each consisting of 10 men, slipped through the walls of Norbulingka while everyone slept. Among them was the 14th Dalai Lama, Tenzin Gyatso, disguised as a soldier. He turned around and looked at Norbulingka, his summer palace. Then 23, he probably didn't know he would never see it again.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Tibet\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-21daf171157a9230dfc615051c70b8da3d0d6612-1280x720-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/21daf171157a9230dfc615051c70b8da3d0d6612-1280x720.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-21T13:15:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"THE TIBETAN PLATEAU | Tibet Private Tour\\nA unique private tour through the Tibetan Plateau, commonly known as the Roof of the World, during the time the Tibetan people celebrate the Shoton Festival. Indulge through this private Tibet tour in the complex world of Tibetan Buddhism while taking in the mesmerizing views of the Himalayas rising high above this elevated plateau.\",\"metaTitle\":\"THE TIBETAN PLATEAU | Tibet Private Tour\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"is-dalai-lama-leader-of-tibet\"},\"tags\":[\"Tibet \",\"Dalai Lama\"],\"title\":\"Is Dalai Lama Leader of Tibet?\"},{\"_id\":\"bb9e3641-1789-4041-ba5f-6636004a4f0a\",\"excerpt\":\"Cambodian Genocide: Pol Pot's reign of terror\\nIn the 2000s, I visited Tuol Song or Hill of Poisonous Trees. The walls of this old school, located on a hilltop, were adorned with pictures of Cambodians tortured to death. While I was looking at their gloomy faces, the laughter of an American girl disturbed my focus. The contrast between the suffering of the victims and her cheerfulness filled my eyes with tears.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Cambodia\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-51b7838205578df5f61af4722dcc31c726103b18-1280x480-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/51b7838205578df5f61af4722dcc31c726103b18-1280x480.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-21T13:15:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"Vietnam and Cambodia are two of the most fascinating countries on the Asian continent, both dramatically affected by recent history. Both countries were heavily affected by the US-led Vietnam war, resulted in counter-revolution, bringing to life the Khmer Rouge in Cambodia and the Viet Minh in Vietnam.\",\"metaTitle\":\"Indochina Delights\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"cambodian-genocide-pol-pot-s-reign-of-terror\"},\"tags\":[\"Cambodia\"],\"title\":\"Cambodian Genocide: Pol Pot's reign of terror\"},{\"_id\":\"f86314c8-3cc8-460c-9c4a-144d6342096e\",\"excerpt\":\"South Korea: Miracle on the Han River\\nOn the morning of May 16, 1961, South Koreans woke up to political turmoil. The army took the hills around the capital with tanks and artillery, threatening to fire government installations. They had soon installed General Park Chung-hee as a de facto ruler. What awaited the new leader was a torn-down nation, suffering through the aftermath of the Korean War that claimed the lives of 2 million people and left millions in poverty.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Han River\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-69a5329ecaccd496f0a6368845cf40a6d31e0029-1280x960-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/69a5329ecaccd496f0a6368845cf40a6d31e0029-1280x960.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-21T13:00:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"KOREAN AUTUMN WALKING TOUR | KOREA PRIVATE TOUR\\nThis Korea private tour celebrates the fusion Korean contemporary culture is all about, from Confucianism to Buddhism through excessive Consumerism and Materialism, and the admiration of the Korean people for the breathtaking natural features surrounding them.\",\"metaTitle\":\"South Korea private trip\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"south-korea-miracle-on-the-han-river\"},\"tags\":[\"South Korea\"],\"title\":\"South Korea: Miracle on the Han River\"},{\"_id\":\"b24f702b-6744-4533-a586-fa6593bbf36c\",\"excerpt\":\"Earlier this month, leaders from 15 Asia-Pacific nations signed a historic deal that would reduce trade barriers in an area covering a third of the world population and a similar share of the global economy. The new free-trade zone is larger than the US-Mexico-Canada Agreement and the European Union. Economists estimate it can add $200 billion annually to the global economy by 2030. The Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) brings together China, Japan, and South Korea in a trade deal for the first time while also including 10 Southeast Asian countries – Brunei, Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, Myanmar, the Philippines, Singapore, Thailand, and Vietnam. Australia and New Zealand are the only non-Asian partners on board, while the US sits on the sidelines.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Asia Pacific and China\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-c56e0193fc008393d5df51e624c1ad907227e3b5-1280x300-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/c56e0193fc008393d5df51e624c1ad907227e3b5-1280x300.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-20T11:00:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"In conclusion, it is critical to point out that the RCEP was not just promoted by Beijing but also by other governments as having immense ramifications in the midst of the financial crisis caused by the COVID-19 pandemic and the anti-free trade approach of the West. It is also further proof of Asia’s growing power. The RCEP is showing us that the global center of economic gravity is pushing relentlessly to the East. The region keeps walking ahead to trade liberalization even as other regions have become more cynical. Regardless, for any of the above predictions to come true, signatories must first ratify the agreement. That could happen by January 2022. Once RCEP is in motion, there is no doubt that countless firms will be able to enter markets that they may never have considered in the past.\",\"metaTitle\":\"China trade deal\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"china-and-asia-pacific-the-largest-trade-deal-in-history\"},\"tags\":[\"China \"],\"title\":\"China \u0026 Asia-Pacific: The Largest Trade Deal in History\"},{\"_id\":\"a3519de4-5607-4659-b122-c523eb87e7ce\",\"excerpt\":\"Unlike the Tibetans or Muslim Uyghurs, China’s ethnic Mongol population has long been seen as a stereotypical “model minority”, due to the lack of visible instances of interethnic conflict. Earlier this month, however, Chinese Mongols, most of whom reside in the Inner Mongolia autonomous region, have strongly protested in opposition to Beijing’s plans to reduce the prominence of the Mongolian language. The government plans to replace Mongolian with Mandarin as the primary medium of teaching for math, history, politics, and literature, although Mongolian language lessons will continue.\\n\\n\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Mongolian Language and Culture\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-1cfb721e3819e06d0b81b54932ce7da7dcb2a1ab-1280x240-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/1cfb721e3819e06d0b81b54932ce7da7dcb2a1ab-1280x240.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-20T10:45:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"Mongolia Private Tour\\nOur Mongolia private tours offer a variety of activities to meet the taste and needs of each of our travelers. These include trekking, horse and camel riding, home and monastery stay, overland and cultural tours, and winter tours for family and friends.\",\"metaTitle\":\"Mongolian Language and Culture\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"the-war-you-never-heard-of\"},\"tags\":[\"Mongolian Language \"],\"title\":\"The war you never heard of\"},{\"_id\":\"814afa86-fd33-499f-9524-78a73c945715\",\"excerpt\":\"Serving as the official seat of 24 emperors of the Ming and Qing dynasties, the Forbidden City holds the world's most extensive collection of Chinese art, consisting of roughly 1.8 million items. Yet the most valuable imperial relics, considered as an epitome of Chinese fine art, are found in Taiwan. Nearly 90 percent of Taipei's National Palace Museum collection was accumulated by the emperors themselves, despite the collection being only a third as big as that of Beijing.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Forbidden City\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-1b3b59c9cfd9a6579a1c7a5fed495df2d78ac8c4-1280x240-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/1b3b59c9cfd9a6579a1c7a5fed495df2d78ac8c4-1280x240.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-20T08:45:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"CHINA DELIGHTS | CHINA PRIVATE TOUR\\nThis China private tour features a well-balanced itinerary between urban and rural, old and new, highlighting past, current, and future events of this mighty giant turned into a global force to be reckoned with. Without a doubt, this 14 days China private tour provides an insight into a country far more complicated than what is portrayed in Western media.\",\"metaTitle\":\"China Private tour\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"lost-treasures-of-a-two-headed-dragon\"},\"tags\":[\"China\"],\"title\":\"Lost treasures of a Two-Headed Dragon\"},{\"_id\":\"cb00a3e1-a422-4871-b27d-9c35381916c1\",\"excerpt\":\"The Communist Party of Kampuchea (CPK), often referred to as the Khmer Rouge, ruled Cambodia from 1975 to 1979. In the course of the four years of its reign, Khmer Rouge enacted one of the worst mass killings of the 20th century. The party introduced policies that overlooked human rights and quickly turned the country into a huge detention center, which later became a graveyard for an estimated two million people.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Cambodia\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-511581d057293ada96c3913f48e4303da9988e1e-1280x240-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/511581d057293ada96c3913f48e4303da9988e1e-1280x240.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-20T08:30:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"INDOCHINA DELIGHTS | CAMBODIA \u0026 VIETNAM PRIVATE TOUR\\nThis 14 days Cambodia and Vietnam private tour takes through the amazing landscapes of these countries, locked between the Mekong River and the South China Sea, providing insight into these ancient cultures, and the impact these major events have had on the people of Vietnam and Cambodia.\",\"metaTitle\":\"Cambodia’s years of Communist terror\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"the-khmer-rouge-monsters\"},\"tags\":[\"Cambodia\"],\"title\":\"The Khmer Rouge Monsters\"},{\"_id\":\"2f456b34-c744-45ee-81df-66d2650e0978\",\"excerpt\":\"The Altai Mountains, one of the most secluded areas in the world, covers a vast area of over 16,000 kilometers, forming an impregnable barrier against globalization with its permanently snow-covered peaks that rise above 4,500m. This land of undiscovered beauty and wilderness is home to the Kazakhs, who have been preserving the ancient tradition of falconry to these days. Although falconry is still popular in many countries, including the United Kingdom and Saudi Arabia, hunting with golden eagles is exclusively a Kazakh practice.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Golden Eagle - The Wings of the Kazakh\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-37dc7d49fe632806e2e5ab797e3a073ef2d42946-1280x480-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/37dc7d49fe632806e2e5ab797e3a073ef2d42946-1280x480.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-20T08:15:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"Golden eagles have an average lifespan of between 20-30 years, but regardless of this, the hunter releases the bird back into the wild after 10 years, to sustain the gene pool. It is a sad moment for both the hunter and the eagle. The hunter takes the bird afar and hides in a place where he can’t be seen or wait for the nightfall to release it, to make sure he would not be followed back home. It is said that even many years after their separation; the hunter thinks about his former companion, wondering if it had survived on its own or if it has managed to build a home for itself. For Kazakh hunters, having an eagle as a mate is like having wings of their own over a human body.\\n\\n\",\"metaTitle\":\"Golden Eagle\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"golden-eagle-the-wings-of-the-kazakh\"},\"tags\":[\"Golden Eagle\",\"Western Mongolia\"],\"title\":\"Golden Eagle - The Wings of the Kazakh\"},{\"_id\":\"20638aac-29a8-4d95-9248-ede5d8f4a632\",\"excerpt\":\"In a modern world where celebrities like Justin Bieber and Beyonce are idolized, the 14th Dalai Lama has managed to become an icon, recognized all over the world as a spokesman for Buddhism. Due to his phenomenal rise to stardom, people often mistake him as THE Dalai Lama. As a matter of fact, most of us don’t know that he is the most recent in a historical linage of spiritual leaders of the Gelug sect in Tibetan Buddhism. Historically, Sonyam Gyatso, the third Dalai Lama was the first one to bear the title in his lifetime. The title Dalai Lama, meaning “Ocean of Wisdom”, was granted to him in 1578 by Altan Khan, a descendant of Genghis Khan who was ruling a large chunk of Central Asia at the time. Since then, till now, his two predecessors and all successors have been carrying the notorious title.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Dalai Lama\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-a9a7b94f7fc89e9f5f1c352b72540bc81fc69d03-1280x300-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/a9a7b94f7fc89e9f5f1c352b72540bc81fc69d03-1280x300.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-20T07:15:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"ACROSS THE TIBETAN PLATEAU | TIBET PRIVATE TOUR\\nA unique journey through the Tibetan Plateau- the Roof of the World as it is commonly known. Come and indulge in the intriguing world of Tibetan Buddhism and lifestyle.\",\"metaTitle\":\"ACROSS THE TIBETAN PLATEAU | TIBET PRIVATE TOUR A unique journey through the Tibetan Plateau- the Roof of the World as it is commonly known. Come and indulge in the intriguing world of Tibetan Buddhism and lifestyle.\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"dalai-lama-a-short-lived-position\"},\"tags\":[\"Dalai lama\"],\"title\":\"Dalai Lama- A short lived position\"},{\"_id\":\"e1341d83-4b4a-446e-88b3-b79aa4e781d6\",\"excerpt\":\"Hailed as the Land of the Thunder Dragon, Bhutan is the only independent country in the world, where Tibetan Buddhism is an official religion of the state. Opening to the outside world only in the 1970s, television and the internet did not come to Bhutan until 1999. Hence, it comes as no surprise that the core values of this small Himalayan nation are strongly influenced by Buddhist ideology.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Bhutanese mask dance- Cham dance\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-29996add3564d8857b700250a12699e66e93cbfd-1280x400-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/29996add3564d8857b700250a12699e66e93cbfd-1280x400.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-20T07:15:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"BHUTANESE DELIGHTS | BHUTAN PRIVATE TOUR\\nJoin us on an in-depth trip through the Kingdom of Bhutan to see for yourself how these far-flung images are so true to reality. Attend the annual Gangtey Festival and see the purest form of traditional Buddhist ceremonies taking place through a buzzing country-fair.\",\"metaTitle\":\"BHUTANESE DELIGHTS | BHUTAN PRIVATE TOUR Join us on an in-depth trip through the Kingdom of Bhutan to see for yourself how these far-flung images are so true to reality. Attend the annual Gangtey Festival and see the purest form of traditional Buddhist ceremonies taking place through a buzzing country-fair.\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"bhutanese-mask-dance\"},\"tags\":[\"Bhutan\",\"Cham dance\"],\"title\":\"Bhutanese mask dance\"},{\"_id\":\"3766d874-87d7-4914-adfa-1344d55932bd\",\"excerpt\":\"China’s paramount leader Xi Jinping said \\\"Over the past 70 years, the Chinese people, with perseverance and strenuous efforts, have achieved rapid development which owes the world. Harsh poverty, which has haunted the Chinese people for thousands of years, will soon become a thing of the past, a great miracle in human history!\\\" on the occasion of the 70th anniversary of the country. But the country’s grandeur history tells a whole different story!\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Hong Kong private tour\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-e49010c5c7cfc2bb26890f09ca2897cef7600256-1280x450-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/e49010c5c7cfc2bb26890f09ca2897cef7600256-1280x450.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-20T07:00:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"Our China Private Tours include the autumn trip Tibetan plateau, adventure along ancient Silk Road, journey in Inner Mongolian Desert, and the introductory trip to the ancient capital of Xian and the current vibrant capital, Beijing and the country’s biggest and superpower resembling city of Shanghai. The middle kingdom reveals its secrets for you!\",\"metaTitle\":\"Our China Private Tours include the autumn trip Tibetan plateau, adventure along ancient Silk Road, journey in Inner Mongolian Desert, and the introductory trip to the ancient capital of Xian and the current vibrant capital, Beijing and the country’s biggest and superpower resembling city of Shanghai. The middle kingdom reveals its secrets for you!\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"china-s-rise-to-superpower\"},\"tags\":[\"China\",\"Hong Kong\",\"Private tour\"],\"title\":\"China's Rise to Superpower\"},{\"_id\":\"b567475a-6e8f-430f-84b1-e02dd8a75ffd\",\"excerpt\":\"The Trans-Siberian Railway\\n\\nThe Trans-Siberian Railway is considered as a geostrategic success evenly matched to the building of the Panama channel. The railway is featured in the Guinness Book of Records for its total length, the number of stations and for the fastest pace of construction, taking only 26 years to complete. By its main route, passengers can travel 9,289 km from Moscow to Vladivostok in just seven days. Its secondary branch, known as the Trans-Mongolian, follows an ancient tea-caravan route from Russia’s capital to Beijing.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"The railway is featured in the Guinness Book of Records for its total length, the number of stations and for the fastest pace of construction, taking only 26 years to complete. By its main route, passengers can travel 9,289 km from Moscow to Vladivostok in just seven days. Its secondary branch, known as the Trans-Mongolian, follows an ancient tea-caravan route from Russia’s capital to Beijing.\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-34fa05029013f8760e1104160ec8edb4ee33b5bd-1280x300-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/34fa05029013f8760e1104160ec8edb4ee33b5bd-1280x300.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-20T07:00:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"TRANS-SIBERIAN INSIDER | PRIVATE TRANS-SIBERIAN TRAIN TOUR\\nAn inspiring combination of the famous Baikal lake and the beautiful Ural Mountains in Russia, the great Gobi Desert in Mongolia, and the historic Great Wall of China will make your Trans-Siberian train tour a memorable experience.\",\"metaTitle\":\"TRANS-SIBERIAN INSIDER | PRIVATE TRANS-SIBERIAN TRAIN TOUR An inspiring combination of the famous Baikal lake and the beautiful Ural Mountains in Russia, the great Gobi Desert in Mongolia, and the historic Great Wall of China will make your Trans-Siberian train tour a memorable experience.\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"the-railway-that-changed-the-course-of-history\"},\"tags\":null,\"title\":\"The railway that changed the course of history\"},{\"_id\":\"c0531a69-6419-404e-9bf7-d8b48bd2d347\",\"excerpt\":\"After wandering for days, a man found himself near a large peepul tree. He decided to sit beneath it and meditate upon his questions. Before long, he felt as if he was floating in space, seeing the world from far, far away. He saw himself. And then, he found an answer. This man would come to be known as Buddha. The answers he found would develop into a religion that amassed half a billion believers worldwide, changing its true color in the process.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"After wandering for days, a man found himself near a large peepul tree. He decided to sit beneath it and meditate upon his questions. Before long, he felt as if he was floating in space, seeing the world from far, far away. He saw himself. And then, he found an answer. This man would come to be known as Buddha. The answers he found would develop into a religion that amassed half a billion believers worldwide, changing its true color in the process.\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-6aeccafe80d76e7ca8b1bf79ac2d24c5c2072156-1280x480-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/6aeccafe80d76e7ca8b1bf79ac2d24c5c2072156-1280x480.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-20T04:30:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"After wandering for days, a man found himself near a large peepul tree. He decided to sit beneath it and meditate upon his questions. Before long, he felt as if he was floating in space, seeing the world from far, far away. He saw himself. And then, he found an answer. This man would come to be known as Buddha. The answers he found would develop into a religion that amassed half a billion believers worldwide, changing its true color in the process.\",\"metaTitle\":\"By adopting a significant amount of cultural values that existed long before Buddha meditated under the peepul tree, Buddhism made itself the dominant religion in East Asia. Possibly inspired by Buddhism's success, other religions also started embracing local customs to gain public support. The best example of such practices would be saints' culture in Latin American Catholicism and Russian Orthodoxy.\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"buddhism-a-chameleon-faith\"},\"tags\":[\"Buddhism\",\"Religion \"],\"title\":\"Buddhism: A Chameleon Faith\"},{\"_id\":\"add21395-3b73-407c-9df3-9cdc74d3621f\",\"excerpt\":\"Buddhists committed to the path to enlightenment (nirvana) must equip themselves with wisdom (prajña) and compassion (karuṇā). Wisdom allows the practitioner to see past external appearances and understand the reason behind one's suffering, while compassion helps them empathize with others.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Buddism, Buddha \",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-8a052d71e822783087aaf1a3edfa5d354c045b3d-1280x480-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/8a052d71e822783087aaf1a3edfa5d354c045b3d-1280x480.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-20T04:15:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"Buddhists committed to the path to enlightenment (nirvana) must equip themselves with wisdom (prajña) and compassion (karuṇā). Wisdom allows the practitioner to see past external appearances and understand the reason behind one's suffering, while compassion helps them empathize with others.\",\"metaTitle\":\"Trip to Asia, Travel to Asia, Asia tourism, Religion, Buddha, Buddhism, Trip with Trips at Asia\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"buddhism-what-is-compassion\"},\"tags\":[\"Buddha\",\"Buddhism\",\"Asia religion\",\"what is Buddhism\"],\"title\":\"Buddhism: What is compassion?\"},{\"_id\":\"c590423e-de3d-4f01-a8d6-8a733c54a074\",\"excerpt\":\"Earth’s biggest and the most populous continent is Asia. It has a population of 4.5 billion and covers 44,579,000 square kilometers (17,212,000 sq mi) including parts of Russia, Kazakhstan and Turkey. Within its regions, a great variety of ethnicity, culture, environment,economy and political systems exist. The Asian Tigers are now shaping the world’s future and thriving to be the next superpowers of the globe. But, on the other hand, there are also many countries that are heavily affected by nagging poverty and rotten corruption.\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"Asia rice field\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-2c62c07cdd760d4f34e90fe3d24c4d11707d4330-1280x300-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/2c62c07cdd760d4f34e90fe3d24c4d11707d4330-1280x300.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-12-19T04:15:00.000Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":null,\"metaTitle\":\"Trip to Asia\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"travel-to-asia\"},\"tags\":[\"Asia \"],\"title\":\"Travel to Asia\"},{\"_id\":\"c405b176-918e-4c64-b3d4-f94dbcb5339d\",\"excerpt\":\"The amazing story on the recovery of the Bengal Tiger population in Nepal\",\"featured\":false,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"The breathtaking landscape of Bhutan showcases the harmony between nature and traditional architecture\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-f0936466167f0a4f61307f21743a6e4ddff8342d-1280x800-jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/f0936466167f0a4f61307f21743a6e4ddff8342d-1280x800.jpg\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-09-08T13:45:43.997Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"Nepal’s tiger population is thriving once more. Discover how conservation efforts, local communities, and mindful travel are helping these majestic animals reclaim their home, and how you can experience it responsibly with Trips@Asia, Trips At Asia \",\"metaTitle\":\"The Tigers Roar Again in Nepal Wildlife Conservation \u0026 Responsible Travel \"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"the-tigers-roar-again-in-nepal\"},\"tags\":[\"Travel\",\"Nepal \",\"Wildlife \"],\"title\":\"The Tigers roar again in Nepal\"},{\"_id\":\"1c408905-58fe-4d31-9f53-c48a924fa181\",\"excerpt\":\"\\n\",\"featured\":true,\"image\":{\"alt\":\"The Nomads of Mongolia with Trips@Asia\",\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-5b39599e47ae1590f06a7b054006e4a622b91de4-1280x480-webp\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/5b39599e47ae1590f06a7b054006e4a622b91de4-1280x480.webp\"},\"crop\":null,\"hotspot\":null},\"publishedAt\":\"2025-09-08T13:45:39.430Z\",\"seo\":{\"metaDescription\":\"Step into Mongolia’s nomadic world, where vast steppes, family gers, and ancient traditions still shape daily life. Learn how Mongolia’s herders live in harmony with nature and discover how our cultural tours bring their stories to life.\",\"metaTitle\":\"The Nomads of Mongolia | Life, Tradition \u0026 Travel with Trips@Asia\"},\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"the-nomads-of-mongolia\"},\"tags\":[\"Culture\",\"Mongolia\",\"Nature\",\"Nomads\"],\"title\":\"The Nomads of Mongolia\"}],\"description\":\"Welcome to the Trips @ Asia Travel articles!\",\"title\":\"Blogs\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"20:[\"$\",\"link\",\"30\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/favicon-16x16.png\",\"sizes\":\"16x16\",\"type\":\"image/png\"}]\n21:[\"$\",\"link\",\"31\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/favicon.ico\"}]\n22:[\"$\",\"link\",\"32\",{\"rel\":\"apple-touch-icon\",\"href\":\"/apple-touch-icon.png\"}]\n23:[\"$\",\"$L25\",\"33\",{}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"26:I[5502,[\"/_next/static/chunks/9f257ff6d9decb7c.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/5de94a3bde687d1f.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/4dae622e7a762c47.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/e493d6fd941de2ab.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/bb05b7b137d9617b.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/b91439db7363f0ed.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/8c9a5f59bb33c8f8.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\",\"/_next/static/chunks/c434c044b92619ed.js?dpl=dpl_GP3u539Bee36Kg46S4F99kbUyqZx\"],\"HeaderClient\"]\n27:T5dc,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Somewhere in the forested hills of Karnali Province, a community of fewer than 150 people continues to move. The Raute have refused settlement into the present generation - foraging, hunting, carving wooden vessels to trade at village margins, and deciding for themselves whether any encounter takes place. This is one of the last genuinely nomadic communities on earth. This trip enters their territory.\nRaute Nomads \u0026 Bardiya Wildlife is a 9-day small group Nepal tour that begins in Kathmandu - a valley built across 2,000 years of dynastic succession - before flying west into Karnali Province, the country's most remote region. The route descends through Tharu forest villages and a Terai town split between Hindu, Muslim, and Chepang communities, before reaching Bardiya National Park, where one of South Asia's most significant conservation recoveries has restored rhinoceros and tiger populations to a riverine forest still crossed by the undammed Karnali River. The return to Kathmandu arrives in time for Bisket Jatra - the Newari New Year festival in Bhaktapur, a five-century tradition - and closes on Sindur Jatra, when vermillion powder turns the valley ceremonial red.\nGuaranteed to depart from just 6 travelers, the group stays small enough to approach the Raute on their own terms, access community visits that do not scale, and move through national park terrain guided by naturalists reading the forest rather than following a route.\nNepal beyond trekking. This is what that means."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"28:T4af,Bhutan is a secluded and mysterious kingdom hidden amidst the Himalayas’ towering peaks. This exciting Bhutan private tour takes you to some of the kingdom’s most intriguing sites for an in-depth exploration of its history, traditions, and unique natural features. The trip is perfectly scheduled to attend the annual Gangtey Festival and experience the purest form of traditional Buddhist ceremonies, set against a buzzing country fair.\n\nThe people of Bhutan are considered the happiest people on Earth. This is partially achieved through the country’s medieval air, a simple way of life, majestic landscapes, and ancient fortresses, highlighting the glorious past of this tiny yet formidable mountain kingdom.\n\nYou can either join this scheduled departure or have us arrange a private Bhutan tour on dates that best suit you.\n\nThe recommended dates for the Bhutan private tour are spring (March to May) and autumn (September to November). Winter is less popular with travelers, but temperatures are surprisingly agreeable. The chance of seeing the Himalayas, forests, and massive historic structures in snow makes it all worthwhile. The summer is the monsoon season, so it should be avoided."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"3:[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"featuredTrips\":[{\"_id\":\"6136b0f4-b2b0-4551-8002-89f119d55de1\",\"datesAndPricing\":null,\"difficulty\":\"Moderate Trek\",\"duration\":\"9 Days\",\"featured\":true,\"featuredImage\":{\"alt\":null,\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-3cb1edc8e5ca1d6fa78f6522474d8f96eed5a2ef-6000x3376-jpg\",\"metadata\":{\"dimensions\":{\"aspectRatio\":1.7772511848341233,\"height\":3376,\"width\":6000},\"lqip\":\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\"},\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/3cb1edc8e5ca1d6fa78f6522474d8f96eed5a2ef-6000x3376.jpg\"}},\"flexibility\":\"Fixed Dates\",\"location\":{\"_id\":\"f24111da-27ff-4bec-9f55-a276e8236f0d\",\"slug\":null,\"title\":\"Nepal\"},\"overview\":{\"description\":\"$27\"},\"priceStartingFrom\":2943,\"seasons\":null,\"slug\":\"nepal-raute\",\"title\":\"Nepal: Nomads, Kingdoms \u0026 Living Goddess\"},{\"_id\":\"7bf91c7b-5599-4b58-bf83-46628b269de0\",\"datesAndPricing\":{\"availableDates\":[{\"dateRange\":{\"end\":\"2026-09-23\",\"start\":\"2026-09-13\"},\"status\":\"available\"},{\"dateRange\":{\"end\":\"2026-11-02\",\"start\":\"2026-10-23\"},\"status\":\"available\"}]},\"difficulty\":null,\"duration\":\"11 Days\",\"featured\":true,\"featuredImage\":{\"alt\":null,\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-355aebbedb3756f5a8bc3b4b24bc48e81abd3e84-6000x4000-jpg\",\"metadata\":{\"dimensions\":{\"aspectRatio\":1.5,\"height\":4000,\"width\":6000},\"lqip\":\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\"},\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/355aebbedb3756f5a8bc3b4b24bc48e81abd3e84-6000x4000.jpg\"}},\"flexibility\":null,\"location\":{\"_id\":\"f8da9f7d-16b2-4223-a136-00218d1c7197\",\"slug\":null,\"title\":\"Bhutan\"},\"overview\":{\"description\":\"$28\"},\"priceStartingFrom\":3058,\"seasons\":[\"autumn\"],\"slug\":\"bhutanese-delights\",\"title\":\"Bhutanese Delights\"},{\"_id\":\"230a17d5-80b6-4cb5-ba70-e2e5ffc5d7c6\",\"datesAndPricing\":{\"availableDates\":[{\"dateRange\":{\"end\":\"2026-06-25\",\"start\":\"2026-06-15\"},\"status\":\"available\"},{\"dateRange\":{\"end\":\"2026-08-10\",\"start\":\"2026-07-31\"},\"status\":\"available\"},{\"dateRange\":{\"end\":\"2026-09-10\",\"start\":\"2026-08-31\"},\"status\":\"available\"}]},\"difficulty\":null,\"duration\":\"11 Days/ 10 Nights\",\"featured\":true,\"featuredImage\":{\"alt\":null,\"asset\":{\"_id\":\"image-4aa9c6f8b2a94ce988b67661d59f05548ce76b0f-1280x480-webp\",\"metadata\":{\"dimensions\":{\"aspectRatio\":2.6666666666666665,\"height\":480,\"width\":1280},\"lqip\":\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\"},\"url\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/ckjf3phx/production/4aa9c6f8b2a94ce988b67661d59f05548ce76b0f-1280x480.webp\"}},\"flexibility\":null,\"location\":{\"_id\":\"7b129441-6540-42d5-9a56-bcd34c0c3bc4\",\"slug\":null,\"title\":\"Mongolia\"},\"overview\":{\"description\":\"A sampling of the best attractions Mongolia has to offer for visitors in one trip, this 11-day tour will take you through the northern edge of the Gobi Desert, the ancient capital of the Mongol Empire at Karakorum, hot springs, volcanoes, rivers, and lakes. Along the way, you will have the chance to meet different ethnic groups and learn about ancient traditions and about the lifestyle of the nomads roaming the vast Mongol steppes.\\n\\nRecommended months for the Best Attractions of Mongolia Tour are May, June, July, August, and September. You could either join one of our scheduled departures or have us arrange your own private tour at dates that best fit you. Please get in touch with us for more details.\"},\"priceStartingFrom\":3367,\"seasons\":null,\"slug\":\"jewels-of-mongolia\",\"title\":\"Jewels of Mongolia \"}],\"headerData\":{\"menu\":[{\"link\":\"/asia-guide\",\"position\":\"right\",\"submenu\":null,\"title\":\"Asia guide\",\"type\":\"link\"},{\"link\":\"/blogs\",\"position\":\"right\",\"submenu\":null,\"title\":\"Blogs\",\"type\":\"link\"},{\"link\"